      "source": [
        "# 🧠 DeepFake Detector - Entrenamiento en Kaggle\n",
        "\n",
        "Este notebook es **100% autónomo**. No necesitas Google Drive.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 📋 Pasos:\n",
        "1. Verificar GPU\n",
        "2. Agregar el dataset `xhlulu/140k-real-and-fake-faces` (Add Data > Search)\n",
        "3. Ejecutar TODAS las celdas en orden\n",
        "4. Descargar el modelo al finalizar\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚠️ IMPORTANTE:\n",
        "- **NO cierres la pestaña** mientras entrena\n",
        "- El entrenamiento tarda ~20-40 min con GPU\n",
        "- El modelo se guardará en `/kaggle/working/`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🔧 Paso 1: Verificar GPU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "print(f\"PyTorch: {torch.__version__}\")\n",
        "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "    print(f\"✅ GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"   Memoria: {torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_mem / 1024**3:.1f} GB\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ NO hay GPU. Ve a Settings > Accelerator > GPU\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📦 Paso 2: Instalar dependencias"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install -q torch torchvision pillow opencv-python-headless numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn tqdm pandas\n",
        "print(\"✅ Dependencias listas!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📂 Paso 3: Configurar rutas del dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "**Primero agrega el dataset:**\n"        "1. En el panel derecho, haz clic en **\"Add Data\"**\n",
        "2. Busca: `xhlulu/140k-real-and-fake-faces`\n",
        "3. Haz clic en **\"Add\"**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import os\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ruta del dataset en Kaggle (ya viene pre-cargado)\n",
        "KAGGLE_DATA = Path('/kaggle/input/140k-real-and-fake-faces')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ruta de trabajo (aquí se guardan los resultados)\n",
        "WORK_DIR = Path('/kaggle/working')\n",
        "DATA_DIR = WORK_DIR / 'data'\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = WORK_DIR / 'outputs'\n",
        "CHECKPOINTS_DIR = OUTPUT_DIR / 'checkpoints'\n",
        "PLOTS_DIR = OUTPUT_DIR / 'plots'\n",
        "\n",
        "# Crear carpetas\n",
        "for d in [DATA_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR, CHECKPOINTS_DIR, PLOTS_DIR]:\n",
        "    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verificar dataset\n",
        "print(f\"Dataset Kaggle: {KAGGLE_DATA}\")\n",
        "if KAGGLE_DATA.exists():\n",
        "    print(f\"  Contenido: {list(KAGGLE_DATA.iterdir())}\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"❌ Dataset no encontrado. Agrega 'xhlulu/140k-real-and-fake-faces' desde Add Data.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📋 Paso 4: Organizar dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "El dataset de Kaggle tiene imágenes en:\n",
        "```\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/train/real/\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/train/fake/\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/valid/real/\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/valid/fake/\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/test/real/\n",
        "real_vs_fake/real-vs-fake/test/fake/\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import shutil\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
        "\n",
        "# Buscar la carpeta correcta dentro de real_vs_fake\n",
        "images_root = None\n",
        "for candidate in [\n",
        "    KAGGLE_DATA / 'real_vs_fake' / 'real-vs-fake',\n",
        "    KAGGLE_DATA / 'real_vs_fake',\n",
        "    KAGGLE_DATA,\n",
        "]:\n",
        "    if (candidate / 'train' / 'real').exists():\n",
        "        images_root = candidate\n",
        "        break\n",
        "\n",
        "if images_root is None:\n",
        "    # Buscar recursivamente\n",
        "    for p in KAGGLE_DATA.rglob('train'):\n",
        "        if (p / 'real').exists():\n",
        "            images_root = p.parent\n",
        "            break\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"📁 Imágenes en: {images_root}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Copiar imágenes\n",
        "splits = {\n",
        "    'train': ('train', 'train'),\n",
        "    'validation': ('valid', 'validation'),\n",
        "    'test': ('test', 'test'),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for dst_name, (src_name, _) in splits.items():\n",
        "    src_dir = images_root / src_name\n",
        "    if not src_dir.exists():\n",
        "        print(f\"❌ No existe: {src_dir}\")\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for cls in ['real', 'fake']:\n",
        "        src_cls = src_dir / cls\n",
        "        dst_cls = DATA_DIR / dst_name / cls\n",
        "        dst_cls.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        if not src_cls.exists():\n",
        "            print(f\"❌ No existe: {src_cls}\")\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        \n",
        "        imgs = [f for f in src_cls.iterdir() if f.suffix.lower() in ('.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png')]\n",
        "        for img in tqdm(imgs, desc=f\"  {dst_name}/{cls}\"):\n",
        "            dest = dst_cls / img.name\n",
        "            if not dest.exists():\n",
        "                shutil.copy2(img, dest)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        count = len(list(dst_cls.glob('*')))\n",
        "        print(f\"  ✅ {dst_name}/{cls}: {count} imágenes\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n📊 Resumen:\")\n",
        "for split in ['train', 'validation', 'test']:\n",
        "    for cls in ['real', 'fake']:\n",
        "        count = len(list((DATA_DIR / split / cls).glob('*')))\n",
        "        print(f\"  {split}/{cls}: {count}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🧠 Paso 5: Definir modelo y entrenamiento"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "import torch.nn as nn\n",
        "import torchvision.models as models\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from PIL import Image\n",
        "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n",
        "from torchvision import transforms\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_auc_score, confusion_matrix\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# ─── Configuración ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "IMG_SIZE = 224\n",
        "BATCH_SIZE = 32\n",
        "NUM_WORKERS = 2\n",
        "EPOCHS = 30\n",
        "LR_CLASSIFIER = 1e-4\n",
        "LR_FINETUNE = 1e-5\n",
        "DEVICE = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"🎮 Dispositivo: {DEVICE}\")\n",
        "if DEVICE == 'cuda':\n",
        "    print(f\"   GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ─── Dataset ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "class DeepFakeDataset(Dataset):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, split, transform=None):\n",
        "        self.samples = []\n",
        "        self.transform = transform\n",
        "        for label, cls in enumerate(['fake', 'real']):\n",
        "            cls_dir = DATA_DIR / split / cls\n",
        "            if cls_dir.exists():\n",
        "                for p in sorted(cls_dir.iterdir()):\n",
        "                    if p.suffix.lower() in ('.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png'):\n",
        "                        self.samples.append((str(p), label))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        reals = sum(1 for _, l in self.samples if l == 1)\n",
        "        fakes = sum(1 for _, l in self.samples if l == 0)\n",
        "        print(f\"  Dataset '{split}': {len(self.samples)} muestras ({reals} reales, {fakes} falsas)\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def __len__(self):\n",
        "        return len(self.samples)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
        "        path, label = self.samples[idx]\n",
        "        img = Image.open(path).convert('RGB')\n",
        "        if self.transform:\n",
        "            img = self.transform(img)\n",
        "        return img, label\n",
        "\n",
        "# ─── Transformaciones ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "train_tf = transforms.Compose([\n",
        "    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n",
        "    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n",
        "    transforms.RandomRotation(15),\n",
        "    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.1, contrast=0.1, saturation=0.1, hue=0.05),\n",
        "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
        "    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "val_tf = transforms.Compose([\n",
        "    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n",
        "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
        "    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "# ─── DataLoaders ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "print(\"\\n📂 Cargando datasets...\")\n",
        "train_ds = DeepFakeDataset('train', train_tf)\n",
        "val_ds = DeepFakeDataset('validation', val_tf)\n",
        "test_ds = DeepFakeDataset('test', val_tf)\n",
        "\n",
        "train_loader = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True, num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True)\n",
        "val_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True)\n",
        "test_loader = DataLoader(test_ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=NUM_WORKERS, pin_memory=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n✅ Datasets listos: {len(train_ds)} train, {len(val_ds)} val, {len(test_ds)} test\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ─── Modelo DenseNet-121 ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "model = models.densenet121(weights=models.DenseNet121_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Congelar primeros bloques\n",
        "for param in list(model.parameters())[:-20]:\n",
        "    param.requires_grad = False\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reemplazar clasificador\n",
        "in_feat = model.classifier.in_features\n",
        "model.classifier = nn.Sequential(\n",
        "    nn.Linear(in_feat, 512),\n",
        "    nn.ReLU(inplace=True),\n",
        "    nn.Dropout(0.3),\n",
        "    nn.Linear(512, 2),\n",
        ")\n",
        "model.to(DEVICE)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Optimizador\n",
        "classifier_params = [p for n, p in model.named_parameters() if 'classifier' in n and p.requires_grad]\n",
        "finetune_params = [p for n, p in model.named_parameters() if 'classifier' not in n and p.requires_grad]\n",
        "\n",
        "optimizer = torch.optim.Adam([\n",
        "    {'params': classifier_params, 'lr': LR_CLASSIFIER},\n",
        "    {'params': finetune_params, 'lr': LR_FINETUNE},\n",
        "], weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
        "\n",
        "scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(optimizer, mode='min', factor=0.1, patience=3, min_lr=1e-7)\n",
        "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "\n",
        "total = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
        "trainable = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\n",
        "print(f\"\\n🧠 DenseNet-121: {total:,} parámetros totales, {trainable:,} entrenables ({100*trainable/total:.1f}%)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🚀 Paso 6: Entrenar (~20-40 min)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import time\n",
        "\n",
        "best_val_acc = 0.0\n",
        "best_val_loss = float('inf')\n",
        "early_stop_counter = 0\n",
        "EARLY_STOP = 7\n",
        "\n",
        "history = {'train_loss': [], 'train_acc': [], 'val_loss': [], 'val_acc': [], 'lr': []}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  🚀 INICIANDO ENTRENAMIENTO ({EPOCHS} épocas)\")\n",
        "print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "start_time = time.time()\n",
        "\n",
        "for epoch in range(EPOCHS):\n",
        "    epoch_start = time.time()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # ── TRAIN ──\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    t_loss, t_correct, t_total = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
        "    for inputs, labels in train_loader:\n",
        "        inputs, labels = inputs.to(DEVICE), labels.to(DEVICE)\n",
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
        "        outputs = model(inputs)\n",
        "        loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        optimizer.step()\n",
        "        t_loss += loss.item() * inputs.size(0)\n",
        "        _, pred = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
        "        t_total += labels.size(0)\n",
        "        t_correct += (pred == labels).sum().item()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    train_loss = t_loss / t_total\n",
        "    train_acc = t_correct / t_total\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # ── VALIDATE ──\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    v_loss, v_correct, v_total = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
        "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "        for inputs, labels in val_loader:\n",
        "            inputs, labels = inputs.to(DEVICE), labels.to(DEVICE)\n",
        "            outputs = model(inputs)\n",
        "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
        "            v_loss += loss.item() * inputs.size(0)\n",
        "            _, pred = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
        "            v_total += labels.size(0)\n",
        "            v_correct += (pred == labels).sum().item()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    val_loss = v_loss / v_total\n",
        "    val_acc = v_correct / v_total\n",
        "    \n",
        "    scheduler.step(val_loss)\n",
        "    lr = optimizer.param_groups[0]['lr']\n",
        "    elapsed = time.time() - epoch_start\n",
        "    \n",
        "    history['train_loss'].append(train_loss)\n",
        "    history['train_acc'].append(train_acc)\n",
        "    history['val_loss'].append(val_loss)\n",
        "    history['val_acc'].append(val_acc)\n",
        "    history['lr'].append(lr)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    print(f\"  Época {epoch+1:2d}/{EPOCHS} | Train Loss: {train_loss:.4f} Acc: {train_acc:.4f} | Val Loss: {val_loss:.4f} Acc: {val_acc:.4f} | LR: {lr:.2e} | {elapsed:.0f}s\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Guardar mejor modelo\n",
        "    if val_acc > best_val_acc:\n",
        "        best_val_acc = val_acc\n",
        "        best_val_loss = val_loss\n",
        "        early_stop_counter = 0\n",
        "        torch.save({\n",
        "            'epoch': epoch,\n",
        "            'model_state_dict': model.state_dict(),\n",
        "            'val_acc': val_acc,\n",
        "            'val_loss': val_loss,\n",
        "        }, CHECKPOINTS_DIR / 'best_model.pth')\n",
        "        print(f\"          ✓ Mejor modelo guardado (val_acc={val_acc:.4f})\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        if val_loss < best_val_loss - 1e-4:\n",
        "            best_val_loss = val_loss\n",
        "            early_stop_counter = 0\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            early_stop_counter += 1\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if early_stop_counter >= EARLY_STOP:\n",
        "        print(f\"\\n  ⏹️ Early stopping en época {epoch+1}\")\n",
        "        break\n",
        "\n",
        "total_time = time.time() - start_time\n",
        "print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  ✅ ENTRENAMIENTO COMPLETADO\")\n",
        "print(f\"{'='*60}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Tiempo total: {total_time/60:.1f} minutos\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Mejor val_acc: {best_val_acc:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Épocas: {len(history['train_loss'])}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📊 Paso 7: Ver resultados"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Gráficos de entrenamiento\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(history['train_loss'], label='Train')\n",
        "axes[0].plot(history['val_loss'], label='Val')\n",
        "axes[0].set_title('Loss')\n",
        "axes[0].legend()\n",
        "axes[0].grid(True)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].plot(history['train_acc'], label='Train')\n",
        "axes[1].plot(history['val_acc'], label='Val')\n",
        "axes[1].set_title('Accuracy')\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "axes[1].grid(True)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[2].plot(history['lr'])\n",
        "axes[2].set_title('Learning Rate')\n",
        "axes[2].set_yscale('log')\n",
        "axes[2].grid(True)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.savefig(PLOTS_DIR / 'training_history.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Evaluación en test set\n",
        "model.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINTS_DIR / 'best_model.pth')['model_state_dict'])\n",
        "model.eval()\n",
        "\n",
        "all_labels, all_preds, all_probs = [], [], []\n",
        "with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "    for inputs, labels in test_loader:\n",
        "        inputs, labels = inputs.to(DEVICE), labels.to(DEVICE)\n",
        "        outputs = model(inputs)\n",
        "        probs = torch.softmax(outputs, dim=1)\n",
        "        _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
        "        all_labels.extend(labels.cpu().numpy())\n",
        "        all_preds.extend(preds.cpu().numpy())\n",
        "        all_probs.extend(probs[:, 1].cpu().numpy())\n",
        "\n",
        "acc = accuracy_score(all_labels, all_preds)\n",
        "auc = roc_auc_score(all_labels, all_probs)\n",
        "cm = confusion_matrix(all_labels, all_preds)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n📋 Métricas en Test Set:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Accuracy: {acc:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  AUC:      {auc:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"\\n  Matriz de confusión:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  {cm}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Guardar métricas\n",
        "metrics = {'accuracy': float(acc), 'auc': float(auc)}\n",
        "with open(PLOTS_DIR / 'final_metrics.json', 'w') as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(metrics, f, indent=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Matriz de confusión\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
        "sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues', xticklabels=['Fake', 'Real'], yticklabels=['Fake', 'Real'])\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Predicción')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Real')\n",
        "plt.title('Matriz de Confusión')\n",
        "plt.savefig(PLOTS_DIR / 'confusion_matrix.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 💾 Paso 8: Descargar modelo\n",
        "\n",
        "Haz clic en **Download** en el panel de Output, o ejecuta la celda de abajo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Verificar archivos guardados\n",
        "print(\"💾 Archivos en /kaggle/working/outputs/\")\n",
        "for f in CHECKPOINTS_DIR.glob('*'):\n",
        "    mb = f.stat().st_size / 1024**2\n",
